<title>JAPAN: Japan govt estimates growth in industry sectors.</title>
<headline>Japan govt estimates growth in industry sectors.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government on Thursday predicted growth for industrial market sectors in Japan as part of its action programme for economic reforms.</p>
<p>The estimate, compiled by the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI), is an outlook based on various economic data and movements in industries and is not a target.</p>
<p>The following is a table of current and future market size by industry, in trillions of yen:</p>
<p>					    Current	 2010</p>
<p> Medical/welfare			   38	     91</p>
<p> Life/culture				20	     43</p>
<p> Information/communication	     38	    126</p>
<p> New manufacturing technology	  14	     41</p>
<p> Distribution				36	    132</p>
<p> Environment				 15	     37</p>
<p> Business support			  17	     33</p>
<p> Marine					 4		7</p>
<p> Biotechnology				1	     10</p>
<p> Urban development			  5	     16</p>
<p> Aviation/aerospace (private sector)  4		8</p>
<p> Energy					 2		7</p>
<p> Human resources			    2		4</p>
<p> *International			     1		2</p>
<p> Housing					1		4</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL				 about 200     about 550</p>
<p>*International includes businesses related to trade, investment, personnel and cultural exchanges with other countries.</p>
</text>
